canonical_claim.statement:
Printed. Supplement A p. 26: 'provided $\{\mu_i(\mathbf Y;d),i\in\mathcal S_N\}$ is uniform $L_2$-NED with size $-4$, so is the transformation $\hat\tau_{i,N}(\mu_1,\mu_0;d)=\Big(\frac{\mathbf Z_i}{Np}-\frac{(1-\mathbf Z_i)}{N(1-p)}\Big)\mu_i(\mathbf Y;d)+\frac1N(\mu_1-\mu_0)-\Big(\frac{\mathbf Z_i\mu_1}{Np}-\frac{(1-\mathbf Z_i)\mu_0}{N(1-p)}\Big)-\tau_i(d;\eta)$. Note $\mathrm E[\hat\tau_{i,N}(\mu_1,\mu_0;d)]=0$.' and '$\mathrm E[\hat\tau_{i,N}(\mu_1,\mu_0;d)|\mathcal F_i(s)]$ is equal to: (57) $\Big(\frac{\mathbf Z_i}{Np}-\frac{(1-\mathbf Z_i)}{N(1-p)}\Big)\mathrm E[\mu_i(\mathbf Y;d)|\mathcal F_i(s)]+\frac1N(\mu_1-\mu_0)-\Big(\frac{\mathbf Z_i\mu_1}{Np}-\frac{(1-\mathbf Z_i)\mu_0}{N(1-p)}\Big)-\tau_i(d)$'.

Corrected statement. Define $\hat\tau_{i,N}(\mu_1,\mu_0;d)=\Big(\frac{Z_i}{Np}-\frac{1-Z_i}{N(1-p)}\Big)\mu_i(\mathbf Y;d)+\frac1N(\mu_1-\mu_0)-\Big(\frac{Z_i\mu_1}{Np}-\frac{(1-Z_i)\mu_0}{N(1-p)}\Big)-\frac{\tau_i(d;\eta)}N$, and replace $-\tau_i(d)$ by $-\tau_i(d)/N$ in (57). Under C1 with $0<p<1$, for all real $\mu_1,\mu_0$:
(a) $\mathrm E[\hat\tau_{i,N}(\mu_1,\mu_0;d)]=0$ for every $i$;
(b) $\sum_{i=1}^N\hat\tau_{i,N}(\mu_1,\mu_0;d)=\hat\tau(\mu_1,\mu_0;d)-\mathrm{AME}(d;\eta)$, where $\hat\tau(\mu_1,\mu_0;d)$ is the class (56) (= (27)); in particular $\sum_i\hat\tau_{i,N}(0,0;d)=\hat\tau_{\mathrm{HT}}(d)-\mathrm{AME}(d;\eta)$;
(c) the summand as printed has expectation $\big(\frac1N-1\big)\tau_i(d;\eta)$. Instance (validator): no interference, $\mu_i(\mathbf Y(\mathbf z);d)=z_i$, $\mu_1=\mu_0=0$, $N=8$, $p=\frac12$: the printed summand has mean $-\frac78$, the corrected one mean $0$.
